## Trigger Scenarios

Apply when reviewing MCP UI resources, App Bridge calls, MCP Apps examples, embedded UI claims, or lesson/task plans involving app-hosted MCP UI.

## Required Controls

- Separate upstream MCP UI/App Bridge behavior from local implementation details.
- Verify source URLs and local code before accepting a claim.
- For UI changes in this repo, also follow `.cursor/rules/ui-shell-standards.mdc`.
- Do not create screenshots, browser logs, install logs, or app output as evidence unless produced by real tools.

## No-Mock Gate

Do not create or accept mock installs, mock tests, fake logs, simulated exit codes, placeholder evidence, fabricated review results, or unsupported source claims. Missing evidence must be `blocked` or `unverified`.

## May Change

- MCP UI/App Bridge review notes, implementation plans, Cursor prompts, and operating-layer docs.

## May Not Change

- Runtime UI code, lesson artifacts, generated screenshots, or Supabase state unless explicitly requested and verified.

## Verifiable Output

Return docs cited, files inspected, checks run, compatibility findings, and blocked or unverified claims.
